sec.p:
Algorithm 1 is a proposed cluster selection method that can reduce inter-cluster communication. The proposed method is based on three cases of the number of required cores and the status of the remaining cores in each cluster. The first case is when the sum of all cores remaining in each cluster equals the number of required cores ($m^{req}_{i}=sum(cluster\_remain\_cores)$
). The second case is when there are more remaining cores in any cluster than the number of required cores ($m^{req}_{i} \leq max(cluster\_remain\_cores)$
). The third case is when there are no more than the number of required cores in any cluster, but the sum of the remaining cores of several clusters is greater than the number of required core ($m^{req}_{i} \lt sum(cluster\_remain\_cores)$
 and $m^{req}_{i} \gt max(cluster\_remain\_cores$
)). Note that, as shown in the flowchart in Fig. 3, it is guaranteed that there is at least a remainder of the number of required cores in the processor when the cluster selection takes place.
